OVERVIEW: Show the printer identity and status the emulator would report

Answers the same question `dicom-print status` asks over the network
(N-GET on the Printer SOP Instance, 1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.17): Printer
Status (2110,0010), Printer Status Info (2110,0020), Printer Name
(2110,0030), Manufacturer and Manufacturer's Model Name — from the
configuration alone. Useful for checking a --config file, and
for confirming what --printer-status failure will make an SCU see.

--format json keys each attribute by its PS3.6 keyword (PrinterStatus,
PrinterStatusInfo, PrinterName, Manufacturer, ManufacturerModelName);
the older keys status, statusInfo, name, manufacturer and model carry
the same values and are deprecated.

USAGE: dicom-printscp status <options>

OPTIONS:
  --port <port>           TCP port to listen on (default: 11113)
  --ae-title <ae-title>   AE title the emulator answers as (default: DCMPRINT)
  --max-associations <max-associations>
                          Maximum concurrent associations (default: 10)
  --idle-timeout <idle-timeout>
                          Seconds an idle association may sit before it is
                          aborted; 0 disables (default: 300)
  --allow-ae <allow-ae>   Calling AE title to accept (repeatable; default:
                          accept all)
  --deny-ae <deny-ae>     Calling AE title to refuse (repeatable; takes
                          precedence over --allow-ae)
  --max-pdu <max-pdu>     Maximum Length of a received P-DATA-TF PDU offered
                          during negotiation (PS3.8 D.1), in bytes (default:
                          65536)
  --accept-color/--no-accept-color
                          Accept the Basic Color Print Management Meta SOP
                          Class (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.18); --no-accept-color
                          offers grayscale only (default: yes)
  --presentation-lut/--no-presentation-lut
                          Accept the Presentation LUT SOP Class
                          (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.23): N-CREATE of Presentation
                          LUT Shape (2050,0020) or a Presentation LUT Sequence
                          (default: yes)
  --annotation-box/--no-annotation-box
                          Accept the Basic Annotation Box SOP Class
                          (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.15): N-SET of Text String
                          (2030,0020) (default: yes)
  --annotation-boxes-per-film <annotation-boxes-per-film>
                          Basic Annotation Box instances created per film box,
                          referenced in Referenced Basic Annotation Box
                          Sequence (2010,0520) (default: 6)
  --push-job-events       Send a Print Job SOP Class (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.14)
                          N-EVENT-REPORT, Event Type Done (3, PS3.4 Table
                          H.4-14), after each N-ACTION
  --film-size <film-size> Film Size ID (2010,0050) to accept (repeatable;
                          default: all). Values (the Defined Term is also
                          accepted): 8x10 = 8INX10IN, 8.5x11 = 8_5INX11IN,
                          10x12 = 10INX12IN, 10x14 = 10INX14IN, 11x14 =
                          11INX14IN, 11x17 = 11INX17IN, 14x14 = 14INX14IN,
                          14x17 = 14INX17IN, 24x24cm = 24CMX24CM, 24x30cm =
                          24CMX30CM, a4 = A4, a3 = A3
  --medium <medium>       Medium Type (2000,0030) to accept (repeatable;
                          default: all). Values (the Defined Term is also
                          accepted): paper = PAPER, clear-film = CLEAR FILM,
                          blue-film = BLUE FILM, mammo-clear-film = MAMMO CLEAR
                          FILM, mammo-blue-film = MAMMO BLUE FILM
  --max-image-boxes <max-image-boxes>
                          Maximum image boxes an Image Display Format
                          (2010,0010) may declare (default: 64)
  --max-image-dimension <max-image-dimension>
                          Largest image dimension accepted in an image box, in
                          pixels (default: 10000)
  --printer-name <printer-name>
                          Printer Name (2110,0030)
  --manufacturer <manufacturer>
                          Manufacturer (0008,0070)
  --model <model>         Manufacturer's Model Name (0008,1090)
  --serial-number <serial-number>
                          Device Serial Number (0018,1000)
  --software-version <software-version>
                          Software Versions (0018,1020)
  --printer-status <printer-status>
                          Printer Status (2110,0010) reported to N-GET, PS3.3
                          Table C.13-9: normal = NORMAL, warning = WARNING,
                          failure = FAILURE
  --status-info <status-info>
                          Printer Status Info (2110,0020), a PS3.3 C.13.9.1
                          Defined Term such as SUPPLY EMPTY; empty uses the
                          status's own term
  --dpi <dpi>             Rasterization resolution of the composed sheet
                          (default: 600)
  --density <density>     Density interpretation: paper, film, gsdf (default:
                          paper)
  --margin-mm <margin-mm> Sheet margin in millimetres (default: 5)
  --cell-spacing-mm <cell-spacing-mm>
                          Gap between image cells in millimetres (default: 2)
  --annotations/--no-annotations
                          Draw Basic Annotation Box text on the sheet (default:
                          yes)
  --trim-marks/--no-trim-marks
                          Print a trim box around each image when Trim
                          (2010,0140) is YES, PS3.3 Table C.13-3 (default: yes)
  --max-pixels <max-pixels>
                          Cap on the composed bitmap's longest side, in pixels
                          (default: 12000)
  --output <output>       Film output: png, tiff, pdf, none (repeatable)
  --output-dir <output-dir>
                          Directory written films are saved to (default:
                          ~/Downloads/DICOMKit Films)
  --name-pattern <name-pattern>
                          File-name pattern; tokens {job} {session} {film} {ae}
                          {index} {timestamp}
  --paper-queue <paper-queue>
                          Spool film to this CUPS queue (requires
                          --allow-paper; empty uses the system default queue)
  --allow-paper           Enable paper spooling. Required for --paper-queue to
                          have any effect.
  --open                  Open each written film in the default viewer
  --config <config>       Settings file to read (default:
                          ~/.config/dicomkit/printscp.json when it exists)
  --save-config           Write the resolved settings back to the configuration
                          file and exit
  --format <format>       Output format: text, json (values: text, json;
                          default: text)
  -v, --verbose           Show the full resolved configuration
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

